---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About · intercate"
  description="Technology Adviser. AI governance, digital policy, and university lecturer."
>
  <div class="content-container animate-in">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="section-label">About</span>
      <h1>Andrew Morrison</h1>
      <div class="divider"></div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose about-prose">

      <p>
        My current work sits at the intersection of practical AI deployment and public accountability —
        how do you build agentic systems that actually work for citizens, at scale, within the
        constraints of government? That question drives most of what I think about.
      </p>

      <h2>Advisory and Interest Roles</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Adjunct Associate Professor</strong> — Teaching AI in healthcare and enterprise AI
          topics at postgraduate level (Charles Darwin University), with a focus on human-centred design and responsible
          AI systems.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Background</h2>

      <p>
        My career spans Queensland and federal government digital transformation. I have a
        long-standing interest in open-source tooling, self-hosted infrastructure, and the
        practical craft of building things.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm pursuing an Executive Master of Technology Management at UTS, with coursework
        spanning AI for enterprises, cybersecurity analytics, and technology leadership.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>

      <p>
        This is where I write about things I can share: AI governance thinking, university
        assignments and reflections, and technical topics I'm
        exploring. It's built with Astro and hosted on GitHub Pages.
      </p>

      <p>
        I write in the open because the ideas get better when you have to explain them clearly,
        and because the public sector needs more practitioners sharing what they've learned.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>

      <p>
        The views expressed on this website are solely those of the author in a personal
        capacity and do not represent the views or positions of any current or former employer,
        affiliated organisation, or professional body. This site is maintained independently for
        the purposes of personal reflection, idea development, and the sharing of lived
        experience. You can read the full statement on the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer page</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="connect">
        <h2>Connect</h2>
        <p>The best place to find me is LinkedIn.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrewnmorrison/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="linkedin-share"
        >
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
            <path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433a2.062 2.062 0 01-2.063-2.065 2.064 2.064 0 112.063 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/>
          </svg>
          Connect on LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
.page-header { padding: 4rem 0 1rem; }
.page-header h1 { margin: 0.75rem 0; }

.about-prose { padding-bottom: 6rem; }

.about-prose ul {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
}

.about-prose ul li {
  padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  background: var(--bg-surface);
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.about-prose ul li strong { color: var(--text-primary); }

.connect { margin-top: 3rem; }
.connect h2 { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
.connect p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
</style>
